\subsection{Professional Experience and Technical Qualifications}

Mr.~Amin brings 30+ years of enterprise AI, data science, optimization, and large-scale systems integration experience to the proposed effort. His career spans strategic leadership, hands-on engineering, and applied research across defense-relevant and commercial sectors, including aviation, financial services, transit, and federal systems.

\textbf{Leadership Highlights:}

\begin{itemize}
\item Former Principal Data Science Strategist and Engineering Leader at DXC Technology, where he led the global AI Guild of 10,000+ members and directly supervised 40+ analytics and data-science personnel across multiple delivery centers.
\item Architected custom Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) gate-assignment optimizers for commercial aviation partners, yielding estimated potential cost savings of \$20M--\$40M through improved resource utilization and operational scheduling.
\item Led SAS-to-PySpark platform modernizations for tier-1 financial and transit organizations, designing streaming analytics pipelines, real-time event-processing architectures, and cloud-native data platforms.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Relevance to ARM26TX04-NV001}

Mr.~Amin's background in optimization, streaming analytics, embedded systems, and secure AI delivery directly supports the proposed work for advanced digital-twin and edge-AI capabilities. His experience bridging high-level machine-learning strategy with low-level embedded implementation ensures the technical approach will be both rigorous and executable within constrained operational environments.

\subsection{Intellectual Property Estate}

Mr.~Amin is the \textbf{Sole Inventor} of six Provisional Patent Applications (PPAs I--VI), culminating in \textbf{Patent Pending} USPTO Provisional Patent Application VI (Serial No.~64/124,094, Confirmation No.~2105, Priority Date August~1, 2026, Attorney Docket \textbf{RELU-001-PPA6}), held by Atelier Logic Group LLC dba ReluLayer\texttrademark. The PPA VI specification incorporates by reference in their entireties all prior provisional filings (PPA I--PPA V). This portfolio reflects sustained invention in deterministic embedded safety systems, fixed-point projection engines, and hardware-in-the-loop validation frameworks relevant to the proposed SBIR effort.

