\section{Facilities and Equipment Description}

\subsection{Facility Overview}

The proposed effort will be executed at the physical engineering facility of Atelier Logic Group LLC dba ReluLayer\texttrademark, located at \textbf{32 Normandy Dr., Kenner, LA 70065}. The on-site work utilizes the \textbf{Pacific AI Lab} internal high-performance engineering workstation and testbed environment. The combined facility is a secure, isolated R\&D environment dedicated to embedded AI, digital-twin prototyping, and low-level hardware/software co-design. It provides controlled access, conditioned workspace, and a zero-egress network segment for hardware-in-the-loop testing.

\subsection{Embedded Hardware Rigs}

Atelier Logic Group LLC dba ReluLayer\texttrademark\ maintains multiple ARM Cortex-M7 evaluation platforms at the 32 Normandy Dr. facility, operated within the Pacific AI Lab workstation environment, for prototyping, profiling, and verification of embedded AI and control routines:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{STM32H743BIT6} evaluation boards (ARM Cortex-M7 @ 480 MHz, 2 MB Flash, 1 MB RAM) for real-time deterministic control and low-latency inference experiments.
\item \textbf{Pixhawk 6X} flight-controller platforms, used as reference hardware for embedded autonomy, sensor fusion, and safety-critical software workflows.
\item Supporting power, interconnect, and breakout peripherals for GPIO, SPI, I2C, UART, and ADC test points.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Debugging and Emulation Equipment}

The lab is equipped with professional-grade debugging and signal-analysis tools:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{SEGGER J-Link Ultra+} high-speed debug probes for ARM Cortex-M trace and flash programming.
\item \textbf{ST-Link V3} probes for STM32 on-chip debugging, programming, and virtual COM-port telemetry.
\item \textbf{USB-Saleae 16-channel} high-speed logic analyzers for protocol capture, timing verification, and edge-case diagnosis.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Development Environment and Toolchain}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Software Stack:} `\#![no\_std]` Rust toolchain with embedded-hal, cortex-m, and real-time interrupt-driven frameworks; Python/PySpark for data science and offline model training; Tectonic/LaTeX build pipeline for documentation generation.
\item \textbf{Compute:} High-core-count workstations with CUDA-capable GPUs for model training, simulation, and digital-twin validation; isolated storage for SBIR-controlled technical data.
\item \textbf{Security:} Isolated zero-egress hardware test rig; version-controlled source under encrypted repositories; access-controlled lab environment.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Availability}

All listed facilities, hardware, and equipment are owned and operated by Atelier Logic Group LLC dba ReluLayer\texttrademark\ and are available for the duration of the proposed SBIR effort without additional lease or rental costs. No third-party facility access is required to execute the proposed technical work.

